      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should look into variables related to neighborhood density and socioeconomic status, as these often correlate with different risk profiles. For instance, the concentration of specific types of housing or the average income level in a sector can be strong indicators of potential claim frequency. Furthermore, data on local community characteristics, such as the prevalence of certain types of businesses or the age of the housing stock, can reveal underlying risks that pure financial data misses. These proxies can help you capture the latent patterns you are seeking.",
